 "title": "Groups and their items, an open set",
 "caption": "It stands in a rail, the navigation and the content attached, at the body's full width: the rail stands shut to its icons, and on a phone one bar stands at the top. The page level holds the title. A module may add a record type, so the groups are a list and never a row of tabs. The groups are the lines of a list, with a line between each two, and the chosen one has a band behind it. At a desktop the list stays in view beside the items of the chosen group, which are a plain table here: a few fields, each with two facts. The chosen group is the title of the container at the right, and the action that adds an item stands in its header. On a tablet and a phone one part shows at a time: the items of the chosen group take the place of the list, with a back action before the title, and the list is the screen before it. On a phone the items are the lines of a list, since a plain table gives way to a list there.",
